codex
The count is twelve width-guard blocks and ten direct calls to `reassert_interrupts()` across three functions. GENCTL has no value guard and stores every byte pattern. The remaining exit handles unsupported interrupt callback lines; registration exposes sixteen line IDs, but these files do not establish which unsupported IDs a connected device can actually emit.
